WEBVTT

00:00:58.662 --> 00:01:00.371
It’s the rhetoric of politicians

00:01:00.412 --> 00:01:03.037
debating a new law by imagining
the impact it might have

00:01:03.079 --> 00:01:06.413
like when Ronald Reagan warned
that the introduction of Medicare

00:01:06.454 --> 00:01:09.496
would lead to a socialist future
spent telling our children

00:01:09.538 --> 00:01:14.829
and our children’s children what it once
was like in America when men were free.

00:01:16.079 --> 00:01:19.788
But it’s also the rhetoric of activists
urging change,

00:01:19.829 --> 00:01:21.829
such as Martin Luther King Jr’s dream

00:01:21.871 --> 00:01:24.079
that his children will one day
live in a nation

00:01:24.121 --> 00:01:26.829
where they will not be judged
by the colour of their skin

00:01:26.871 --> 00:01:28.954
but by the content of their character.

00:01:28.996 --> 00:01:32.746
In both cases, the speaker presents
their audience with a possible future